WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.652
A strong OSINT workflow begins with a defined question and ends with useful intelligence for an authorized audience.

00:00:09.652 --> 00:00:14.849
The requirement establishes purpose, scope, constraints, and stopping conditions.

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:20.541
The collection plan turns those boundaries into prioritized source activities.

00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:28.708
Collection records URLs, timestamps, context, and approved preservation artifacts while respecting access controls and privacy.

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:34.896
Processing deduplicates, tags, organizes timelines, and maps relationships without losing provenance.

00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:39.598
Facts, claims, assumptions, and judgments remain visibly separate.

00:00:39.598 --> 00:00:44.795
Validation examines origin, timeliness, bias, manipulation, and source independence.

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:51.477
Corroboration relies on genuinely separate evidence, not repeated copies of one claim.

00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:58.159
Analysis tests competing explanations, identifies gaps, avoids confirmation bias, and documents reasoning.

00:00:58.159 --> 00:01:05.831
Reporting answers the requirement with evidence references, calibrated confidence, limitations, and proportionate next steps.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:11.524
Dissemination protects sensitive information, and feedback improves the next cycle.

00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:18.206
Ethics, legal authority, privacy, documentation, and source reliability are not optional extras.

00:01:18.206 --> 00:01:22.413
They are controls embedded throughout the workflow.

00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:33.055
The goal is not maximum collection; it is a defensible answer produced through scoped, lawful, repeatable, and responsible intelligence work.
